      "content": "When a new check's first run finds a large pre-existing debt, ship it ENFORCED against a recorded, shrink-only baseline file (keys without volatile fields such as line numbers) instead of report-only with the enforce flag at 0. New violations fail immediately, the debt is printed as a TODO line at every gate, and the deliberate negative test (inject -> FAIL + non-zero exit -> revert -> PASS + exit 0) still works. Also: choose the negative-test target deliberately -- a first attempt here silently passed because the chosen citation had no adjacent name, which exposed the check's real limit.",
